{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792335411,"nonce":"ndspB5D72vngbHExos839dtXjtQ=","title":"A scene that animates allocates 300 KB a frame, so a page's collector pauses every few seconds","message":"**What was seen**\nOrbiting the banner in a page freezes it for a moment every few seconds. With ASH_GC_STATS=1 each collection from the sixth on takes 94 to 200 ms with 190 to 230 MB live, and each lines up with a 130 to 250 ms gap in the frames the GPU worker receives, about every 8 s. Ash's wasm collector is not generational, so a collection costs the size of the heap (859f6d5, 719a438 are Ash's side).\n\n**What the program does to bring them on**\nAllocation counted by hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated in the page, at 2x:\nidle, the meters running: 300 KB a frame, 18 MB/s.\nidle, the meters stopped: 2 KB a frame.\ndragging, meters stopped: 130 to 200 KB a frame (the scene redrawn, the callouts placed, the leaders drawn).\ndragging, meters running: 430 KB a frame.\nThe meters' two canvases make their paths afresh every frame (`new Path()`, `ctx.line`, `new Stroke`), and the painter found a path's triangles by the Path object, so a path made afresh was tessellated again each frame.\n\n**Done**\nThe painter finds a shape by what its path contains (Path.signature and Path.same, Stroke.same), so an equal path made afresh is the last frame's and has its triangles moved instead of made again. Idle fell from about 300 to 200 KB a frame, measured with the machine loaded.\n\n**Not done**\nWhat is still allocated each frame when the meters run: the Paths, Strokes, Brushes and ops the draw functions make, and the tessellation of the shapes that really change (the speed's arc and its glow). A canvas could keep its static parts, ticks, track and labels, apart from its moving ones, so the static ones are drawn once.\nThe street map's tessellation is 98 MB of the 230 MB that is live (381 000 vertices for a box 316 by 100); simplifying the geometry to a fraction of a pixel, or drawing the map once into a texture, would cut the heap the collector walks by a third or more.","files":null}]}